WEBVTT

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:04.170
I couldn’t forgive myself for my failure.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:07.090
That’s why I wanted to become stronger.

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:11.990
But in the end, I wasn’t able to do anything.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:18.110
I was scolded for my mistake,
and I’m sure I’ve let them down.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:24.900
I caused trouble for my partner who runs by my side and gave her a painful memory.

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:30.000
The things I’ve done, the paths I’ve chosen...

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.020
They all were useless.

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:39.010
Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha StrikerS<i>
will now begin.</i>

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:37.300
What the...?

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:40.720
Oh, Teana, you’re awake?

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:44.680
Dr. Shamal. Where...?

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:47.100
This is the infirmary.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:51.210
Do you remember that you were shot down during the mock battle this afternoon?

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:57.400
Yes.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:03.200
Nanoha’s training magic missiles are well made,
so they shouldn’t have done any damage to your body.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:08.740
Are you hurt anywhere?

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:14.500
No, I’m all right.

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:16.860
It’s past nine!

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:19.520
At night?

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:26.140
You were sleeping very well.
So well that I almost thought you were dead.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:28.800
You haven’t had much sleep lately, have you?

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:31.770
All the stress you’ve accumulated has caught up with you.

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:44.180
Nanoha?

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:49.130
Fate.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:53.330
Teana woke up a little while ago.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:57.020
She came to the office with Subaru to apologize.

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:57.820
I see.

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.020
I told them you were at the training grounds, Nanoha,

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:03.240
and they should talk to you first thing tomorrow morning.

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:05.810
Thank you.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:08.590
But I’m sorry.

00:04:08.590 --> 00:04:14.430
Because of my incompetent supervision, I got you, Fate, and even the two from Lightning involved.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:17.060
I don’t mind.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:20.280
How did Teana and Subaru look?

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:24.700
They looked like they were still in a bit of a bad mood, as expected.

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:31.850
Well, I’ll make sure to talk to them tomorrow morning—to <i>all</i> the forwards.

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:49.100
Type 2 Gadget Drones have appeared over the Eastern Ocean!

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:54.190
There are twelve units this time.
They’re flying in a circular pattern.

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:55.580
Any Relic signatures?

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:58.770
At this point, there are no responses in the vicinity.

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:00.190
However, this is...

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:02.740
The targets’ speed is a little bit—

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.270
no, <i>much</i> faster than the ones before!

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:14.540
My, this is unusual.

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:18.350
I am delighted that you’re contacting me.

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:20.960
What happened to Zest and Agito?

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:23.120
They’re on a separate operation right now.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:29.040
It seems some of your toys are flying in the distant sky, Doctor.

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:31.890
Soon, you should be able to see some beautiful fireworks.

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:33.310
Relics?

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:37.220
If there were, I would have reported to you from the start.

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:41.000
This is just a performance test of my toys.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:44.360
I want to gather some data on how they get destroyed.

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:45.920
They’re getting destroyed?

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:51.660
I’m not expecting these scraps of metal
to become a force instantly.

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:57.620
They’re just junk I’m using as decoys,
so that my work can shine more brilliantly.

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:03.040
I see. If it’s not a Relic,
then it has nothing to do with me.

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:06.510
However, I wish you luck, Doctor.

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:10.430
Thank you, my sweet Lutecia.

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:12.910
Well then, good day.

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:20.310
My works are indeed well made.

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:25.740
Out of the Type 2 aerial units, there are three groups of four and one group of twelve.

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:28.020
There are no changes since the they were discovered:

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:31.200
each group is flying in its own low, circular pattern.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:34.150
They’re located over the sea in the middle of nowhere.

00:06:34.150 --> 00:06:39.150
There are no signs of a Relic, nor of any
maritime facilities or boats within the vicinity.

00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:42.380
It’s as if they’re asking us to shoot them down.

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:46.800
Indeed. Enforcer Testarossa-Harlaown, what do you make of this?

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:53.470
If Scaglietti is responsible, then he probably wants to see what move we’ll make to test our aerial forces.

00:06:54.290 --> 00:07:00.000
In this situation, we can finish them off by throwing an extreme-range attack at them.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.940
One blast would do it!

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:06.860
Yes, but that’s precisely why we shouldn’t show our hand.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:08.060
Realistically speaking,

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:13.060
we can’t really lift the captains’ limiters for something at this level, anyway.

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:15.780
Instructor Takamachi, what about you?

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:18.770
If the intent is to investigate our military forces,

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:21.280
we should prevent them from attaining any new information

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:25.000
and take care of them the way we always have, right?

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:28.090
We’ll go with that then.

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:38.890
As it’s an aerial fight this time, the three of us, Captain Fate, Lt. Vita, and myself, will sortie.

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:41.600
The rest of you will be on standby in the lobby.

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:44.860
Signum will be taking command there.
Guard the place while we’re gone.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:45.620
Yes, ma’am!

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:46.270
Yes, ma’am.

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:52.810
Oh, and Teana?

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:57.100
Teana, I think I’ll dismiss you for the day.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:04.780
I think that’s a good decision. You’re dismissed.

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:08.420
After all, your physical condition and magical powers aren’t at their best tonight.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:10.340
Someone who won’t listen to you

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:13.970
is someone you can’t use, right?

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:18.320
You said it yourself, and you still don’t understand?

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:20.120
That much is obvious.

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:26.480
I’ve been obeying orders at the scene,
and I haven’t been slacking off during training, either.

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:28.800
Even outside of combat and training,

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:32.380
does the amount of effort I put in have to be exactly as you dictate?

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:36.640
I’m not an elite like you and the other officers, Nanoha!

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:40.750
I don’t have the same amount of talent as Subaru and Erio,
nor do I have a Rare Skill like Caro.

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:43.060
Even if it means I’m going to push myself,

00:08:43.060 --> 00:08:46.320
I’m not going to get stronger
unless I work myself to the bone!

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:50.150
Signum?

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:51.160
Signum!

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:54.660
Don’t worry, I held back.

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:59.100
Pessimistic fools will only drag you down
if you keep putting up with them.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.020
Vice, are you ready to go?

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:04.440
I’m ready as soon as we have you guys on board!

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:11.320
Teana, you seem like you’re a bit worked up
at the moment, but let’s have a talk once I’m back!

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:13.780
I’m telling you to stop spoiling her!

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:19.620
Erio, Caro, sorry, but please look after them.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:20.990
Y-Yes, ma’am!

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:22.290
We’ll try our best.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:33.340
What an eyesore! Stop behaving like
a spoiled child and return to your quarters.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:36.790
Lt. Signum, I think that’s enough.

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:39.300
Subaru, let’s head to the lobby for now.

00:09:40.130 --> 00:09:41.720
Lt. Signum.

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:42.880
What is it?

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:49.340
I think it’s definitely wrong to disobey orders,

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:55.720
and when I think back to how Tia was acting,
I think it was wrong of me not to stop her.

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:58.840
But,

00:09:58.840 --> 00:10:02.020
is it really so bad

00:10:02.020 --> 00:10:07.670
to try to become stronger by your own means and to try your hardest in a tough situation?

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:14.650
Striving to do your best in your own way—is that also something that shouldn’t be done?

00:10:16.290 --> 00:10:21.260
Training in your own time is a good thing,
and striving to become stronger is also a good thing.

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:24.470
Shari?

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:26.710
Weren’t you on duty?

00:10:26.710 --> 00:10:30.400
Command Sergeant Major Rein is in charge of operations right now.

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:35.490
It just looked like everyone was so tense,
and I couldn’t stand seeing you all like this.

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:40.480
Everyone, would you gather in the lobby?

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:47.470
I’ll explain everything about Nanoha and the meaning behind her training.

00:11:08.530 --> 00:11:09.330
Once upon a time,

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:17.810
there was a girl. She was just an ordinary girl
who knew nothing about magic,

00:11:17.810 --> 00:11:20.680
and she wasn’t the type who would get into a fight.

00:11:21.350 --> 00:11:25.660
She went to school with her friends and was living happily with her family.

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:29.580
She was bound to live the rest of her life like that.

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:34.710
However, there was an incident.

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:42.110
She didn’t attend any kind of school for magic,
nor did she have special skills.

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:45.540
She obtained magical power
from a chance encounter,

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:48.490
and it just so happened that she had great capacity.

00:11:48.490 --> 00:11:50.210
And she was only a nine-year-old girl.

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:55.460
Only a few months after she acquired magic,

00:11:55.460 --> 00:11:58.820
she was thrown into real combat
that put her life at stake.

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:00.040
Is that...?

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:01.240
Fate?

00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:07.820
Fate was going through some complications with her family at the time.

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:11.340
They were fighting each other
over a particular Lost Logia.

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:15.480
The central figure in this incident
was Testarossa’s mother.

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:19.360
The incident, named after her,
is called the Presea Testarossa Incident,

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:21.780
also known as the Jewel Seed Incident.

00:12:28.590 --> 00:12:31.540
A collection bombardment? That large?

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:34.480
By a nine-year-old?

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:39.860
A massive power bombardment puts a lot of strain on the body.

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:44.970
And then, shortly after that,
the battle continued for her.

00:12:48.020 --> 00:12:52.000
An incident we were deeply involved in,
the Book of Darkness Incident.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:56.420
She came close to getting shot down in an assault and was defeated.

00:12:57.370 --> 00:12:59.840
What she chose to overcome that

00:13:01.370 --> 00:13:05.760
was to use the Cartridge System, even though its safety was still questionable at the time.

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:13.790
The Full Drive mode
ignores the strain it puts on the body

00:13:13.790 --> 00:13:16.150
and forcefully generates magic
that surpasses her limit.

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:17.370
Excelion Mode.

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:28.300
In order to save people and to get her will across,
Nanoha continued to push herself.

00:13:28.300 --> 00:13:31.370
704 has arrived in the destination airspace.

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:35.040
Lightning 1, Stars 2, engage.

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:40.320
Okay, Nanoha, take care.

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:42.700
Thanks, Vice.

00:13:42.700 --> 00:13:44.940
Let’s go, Raising Heart.

00:13:44.940 --> 00:13:47.380
All right, my master.

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:59.830
This is Stars 1, assistance with mid-range shots, coming up!

00:13:59.840 --> 00:14:01.270
Roger!

00:14:03.680 --> 00:14:08.780
However, there was no way that repeating such acts wouldn’t take its toll on her body.

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:12.760
There was an accident during the second winter
after she entered the Bureau.

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:16.460
It happened while she was returning from an investigation mission

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:20.490
on another world with Vita and some others.

00:14:20.490 --> 00:14:22.880
An unidentified object appeared suddenly.

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:27.650
It was an opponent that Nanoha wouldn’t have had any problems protecting her allies from

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:29.610
or destroying if she were her usual self.

00:14:29.610 --> 00:14:32.510
But the stress that she had been under

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:39.110
and the way she kept pushing herself made Nanoha slightly less capable.

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:42.210
The result was this.

00:14:44.440 --> 00:14:51.780
Nanoha apologized to us for pushing herself too far and kept smiling in front of us, but

00:14:53.780 --> 00:15:00.360
having been told that she might not be able to walk again, let alone be able to fly...

00:15:00.360 --> 00:15:02.170
I can’t imagine how she must have felt.

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:10.040
There are battles that must not be lost,
even if it means being reckless or even risking your life.

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:14.340
However, the time when you missed that shot,

00:15:14.340 --> 00:15:16.220
was that a situation where you had to shoot,

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:20.160
even if it meant risking the safety or life of your comrade?

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:30.050
Using a move like that during training,
just whose sake was that for?

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:34.070
What was it for?

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:44.880
Nanoha doesn’t want any of you to go through what she did.

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:48.400
So that you don’t have to push yourself,

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:53.680
and to be absolutely, positively sure that you come back safe and sound.

00:15:56.320 --> 00:16:01.730
She has been training you with care,
thinking about your safety the whole time.

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:09.280
Vita, take care of that last one!

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:11.260
Of course!

00:16:11.260 --> 00:16:13.920
Let’s go, Eisen! Form Zwei!

00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:15.740
Explosion

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:18.680
Rocket Form

00:16:20.570 --> 00:16:23.900
<b>Rocket Hammer</b>

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:35.180
Stars 2 shot down the twenty-fourth unit.
All targets have now been destroyed.

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:36.510
No reinforcements detected.

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:42.220
Contact the nearby maritime observation units to collect the remains.

00:16:42.220 --> 00:16:42.730
Roger!

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:47.770
It seems there’s no need for them to be on standby there, so can we have the three of them return?

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:51.440
Yes, and we can dismiss the forward unit too.

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:07.000
I-I’m sorry!

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:12.240
Shari, you shouldn’t talk about
other people’s pasts without asking first.

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:14.740
It’s not good for women to be too talkative, you know.

00:17:14.740 --> 00:17:18.390
Well, you know, I just couldn’t stand watching them.

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:21.300
Well, they would have found out about it sooner or later.

00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:24.980
Shari, do you know where Teana is right now?

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:27.540
She’s probably...

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:56.340
I heard a lot from Shari and Lt. Signum.

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:58.800
A record of Nanoha’s failures?

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:00.820
That’s not what...!

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:04.340
About how it’s dangerous to act so recklessly, right?

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:06.730
I’m really sorry.

00:18:14.710 --> 00:18:19.270
Well, now that you understand, I’ll comment about it a bit.

00:18:19.270 --> 00:18:21.920
You know, Teana, you call yourself mediocre

00:18:21.920 --> 00:18:25.680
and say you can’t do anything but shooting and illusion spells,

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:28.420
but you know that’s not true.

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:33.970
You and the others are like ore right now, Teana.

00:18:33.970 --> 00:18:38.340
You have a lot of rough edges,
and it’s hard to tell what your true values are.

00:18:39.040 --> 00:18:44.310
But as you polish up, you’ll start seeing parts that shine.

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:47.270
Erio has his speed.

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:50.270
Caro has her gentle support spells.

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:53.730
Subaru has her explosive power at close range.

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:59.140
And you, Teana, who leads the other three,
can protect them with your shooting and illusion spells

00:18:59.140 --> 00:19:02.320
and can get through any situation with your courage and wits.

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:08.790
That’s an ideal team, and it’s slowly starting to form.

00:19:10.490 --> 00:19:14.460
During the mock battle,
didn’t you notice when you were shot?

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:16.480
When shooting spells are used properly, Teana,

00:19:16.480 --> 00:19:21.050
they’re incredibly hard to evade and really hurt when they hit.

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:28.800
You ignored your most important aspect
and rushed to do something else.

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:30.930
That’s why a situation like that happened.

00:19:30.930 --> 00:19:34.140
That’s what I wanted to teach you.

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:41.080
Then again, your line of thought wasn’t completely wrong either, Teana.

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:44.990
System limiter: test mode release.

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:46.440
Yes.

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:49.420
Try commanding him into Mode II.

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:55.250
Mode II

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:57.660
Set up. Dagger Mode.

00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:06.540
This is...

00:20:06.540 --> 00:20:08.760
Teana, you plan to become an Enforcer, right?

00:20:08.760 --> 00:20:12.440
After you leave here and pursue your path to become an Enforcer,

00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:15.500
you’ll end up fighting one-on-one battles.

00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:18.130
I had this prepared with your future in mind.

00:20:27.920 --> 00:20:31.900
I was thinking of training you on both close and long-range combat for a while now.

00:20:31.900 --> 00:20:36.320
But there’s always the possibility that we’ll sortie anytime, right?

00:20:36.320 --> 00:20:43.300
So I wanted to make sure you’re confident with the skill you excel at the most now.

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:47.030
But my training is a bit dull,

00:20:47.030 --> 00:20:52.470
so you felt you weren’t accomplishing much and having a tough time, weren’t you?

00:20:52.470 --> 00:20:53.250
I’m sorry.

00:20:57.980 --> 00:21:04.910
I’m sorry!

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:15.460
Good morning!

00:21:17.160 --> 00:21:18.380
Morning.

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:22.080
Good morning.

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:24.220
Were you able to sleep well?

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:25.880
Yes, ma’am.

00:21:27.670 --> 00:21:33.300
You’re aware that high-level mages with
excellent combat skills are referred to as <i>aces,</i> right?

00:21:33.300 --> 00:21:38.270
But do you know of another kind of excellent mage and what we call them?

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:44.540
If one of those is present, it’s possible to get through even the toughest situation.

00:21:44.540 --> 00:21:47.980
It’s possible to overcome even the most intense situation.

00:21:47.980 --> 00:21:51.180
Someone with that kind of reliability is called by this name:

00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:55.040
<i>Striker.</i>

00:21:56.560 --> 00:22:00.480
Since the start of your training,
Nanoha has been saying,

00:22:01.390 --> 00:22:06.380
“The four that we have, all of them should be able to become first-class strikers.”

00:22:09.500 --> 00:22:16.520
“So I’ll train them very strictly,
but carefully and thoroughly too.”

00:22:18.940 --> 00:22:23.530
Instructors have a hard time of things, don’t they?

00:22:23.530 --> 00:22:26.380
Even if you train them during difficult times,

00:22:26.380 --> 00:22:30.730
they still end up going their own ways afterwards.

00:22:30.730 --> 00:22:36.580
Well, it’s a bit sad that we can only spend a short amount of time together.

00:22:37.150 --> 00:22:40.000
I can’t look after them forever.

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:45.090
So while I can be with them, I want to teach them as many things as I can.

00:22:47.290 --> 00:22:52.500
Good morning!

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:55.110
Oh, you guys are here.

00:22:55.110 --> 00:22:55.990
Morning.

00:22:55.990 --> 00:22:57.390
Did you sleep well?

00:22:57.390 --> 00:22:58.450
Yes, ma’am!

00:22:58.450 --> 00:23:00.540
All right, I’m gonna train you hard again today!

00:23:00.540 --> 00:23:02.520
No matter what happens,

00:23:02.520 --> 00:23:05.800
no matter who comes around,
I’m not going to let anyone shoot them down.

00:23:06.860 --> 00:23:14.160
Not only while they’re around me,
but when the time comes for them to fly on their own as well.

00:23:21.100 --> 00:23:24.180
Well, let’s put everything into our morning training!

00:23:24.180 --> 00:23:25.040
Yes, ma’am!

00:25:17.280 --> 00:25:18.780
Ordinary days have returned

00:25:18.780 --> 00:25:22.040
with good news
for the forwards.

00:25:22.040 --> 00:25:24.830
All four of them are getting a day off!

00:25:32.000 --> 00:25:35.090
To a fun vacation day, take off!
